# UI & Styling Guidelines

- Build UIs with MUI v7 primitives plus Tailwind utility classes where helpful. Keep the custom theme (rounded corners, shadowless surfaces) in mind and prefer theme tokens (`theme.palette.primary.main`, etc.) over hardcoded colors unless copying existing design language.
- Shared building blocks reside in `src/components/shared` (e.g., `SearchInput`, `StatCard`, `StatusBadge`). Reuse them before introducing duplicates.
- Complex pages are composed by module folders (e.g., `components/modules/orders-page`). Add new subcomponents there to keep domain logic grouped.
- For modals, reuse `src/components/Modal/MyModal.tsx`. It standardizes size props and close affordances; do not instantiate MUI `Dialog` directly unless a requirement deviates significantly.
- Dummy data can be imported from `src/datas/dummies` for UI development, but clearly mark future API touchpoints with TODO comments to ease backend integration.
